-- title:
--   Recognition of 𝒪[[T]] among complete local 𝒪-algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete and separated for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_O$, and let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring, complete and separated for the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic topology, equipped with an $O$-algebra structure. Assume: (i) the composite of the structure map $O \to R$ with the residue map $R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ is surjective, so that the residue field of $R$ is generated by the image of $O$; (ii) there is an element $t \in R$ with
--   $$\mathfrak m_R = \mathfrak m_O R + (t) + \mathfrak m_R^2,$$
--   the sum being taken inside the ideal lattice of $R$, where $\mathfrak m_O R$ denotes the image ideal of $\mathfrak m_O$ under $O \to R$ (in particular $t \in \mathfrak m_R$); and (iii) $2 \le \operatorname{ringKrullDim} R$, the Krull dimension being taken in $\mathbb{Z} \cup \{\pm\infty\}$. Then the type of $O$-algebra isomorphisms $R \simeq O[[T]]$ is nonempty: $R$ is isomorphic, as an $O$-algebra, to the formal power series ring in one variable over $O$.
--
--   This is a recognition criterion for the one-variable formal power series ring over a complete discrete valuation ring: a complete Noetherian local $O$-algebra with the same residue field, relative cotangent space spanned by a single element $t$ modulo $\mathfrak m_O$, and Krull dimension at least two, is $O[[T]]$. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of the deformation rings occurring in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the argument, where a prorepresenting ring is shown to be either a power series ring or a crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_nonempty_algEquiv_powerSeries_of_maximalIdeal_eq_sup_span_singleton_sup_sq_of_two_le_ringKrullDim.lean

